eratorname{cot}⁡x}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(-{csc}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡x}{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573894 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573894 #edb/ref 1069 "q-340610" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573894 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573894 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the derivative of $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot ($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573894 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "70b7e2f2-9311-56ba-8d2d-9b32371b2429" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573894 #edb/ref 1074 "We calculate the derivative using the product rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡(x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573900 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573900 #edb/ref 1069 "q-314291" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573900 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573900 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the slope $m$ of $y=g(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ if $g(x)=-4{e}^{x}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+6.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573900 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7ecca825-7d5a-5032-8595-2b767ed0d377" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573900 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we calculate the derivative using the product rule and sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(-4{e}^{x}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{d}{dx}(-4{e}^{x})\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x+(-4{e}^{x})\\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+\\frac{d}{dx}(6) \\\\  & =-4{e}^{x}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+(-4{e}^{x})(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)+0 \\\\  & =-4{e}^{x}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+4{e}^{x}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\  & =-4{e}^{x}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x(1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and evaluate the slope $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={g}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-4{e}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})(1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =-4{e}^{\\pi /2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573927 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573927 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104314" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573927 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573927 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=\\frac{5-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573927 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cdd054fb-7789-52a0-9a24-44d711412a5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573927 #edb/ref 1074 "We calculate the derivative using the quotient rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x){e}^{x}-(5-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x){e}^{x}}{({e}^{x})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}(2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-5+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)}{{e}^{2x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-5}{{e}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573943 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573857 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573943 #edb/ref 1069 "q-313721" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573943 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573943 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${g}^{′}(x)$ if $g(x)=3\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$\n\n${g}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573943 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f25a3394-05aa-5c37-ad51-535ad5e51912" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573943 #edb/ref 1074 "We take the derivative of each term and then add them, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =3(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
